<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43176" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑτερο-μήκης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ες</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with sides of uneven
			length</i>, i.e. <i>oblong</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				7.14
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑτερόμηκες, τό</span>, <i>oblong rectangle</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Cat.</u>
				11a10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>de An.</u>
				413a17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Euc.
				1
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Def.</u>
				22
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of numbers,
				<i>not square</i>, i.e. produced by the multiplication of two
				<i>unequal</i> factors, as <i><span class="en">
				6
			</span></i>
			=
			<i><span class="en">
				3 x 2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				148a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.367f
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσόπλευρος</span> (both of
			line and number), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>APo.</u>
				73b1
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
